          "text": "8. Seven Rules Recap"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Order by change frequency; manifests before source",
            "Clean in the same RUN; ship artifacts via multi-stage",
            "Ignore aggressively; pin base digests; never run as root",
            "Commit lockfiles; `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` for determinism",
            "`BUILDKIT_INLINE_CACHE=1` where repeatability matters"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "A Stack Of Diffs",
          "text": "An image is a cache-friendly stack of diffs. You optimize it by controlling what changes, how often, and at which layer."
